{# The replays the MLflow store lacks: shown from the replay ledger (report/ledger.py), labelled. #}
{% from 'sentences.en.md.j2' import VERDICT, LABEL, OUTCOME, recs_list %}
{% set REC = {'retrain': 'retrain', 'recalibrate': 'recalibrate the intervals', 'investigate_data': 'investigate the data'} %}
{% macro recorded_block(departures) %}
{% for d in departures if d.recorded %}
**Recorded in the ledger, not re-run here.** Replay `{{ d.id }}` (rules of commit `{{ d.freeze_commit|short }}`) is not in this copy's MLflow store: its MAPE of {{ d.summary.mape.mean|pct(2) }}, its coverage of {{ d.summary.coverage.mean|pct(1) }} and its recommendations ({% for x in d.recommendations %}week of {{ x.week_start }}: {{ REC[x.recommendation] }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% else %}none{% endfor %}) come from its entry in `docs/replay-ledger.json`, written from its run; it was not re-run here.

{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}
{# A v2 replay of record (v2's first 2024 replay, the 2025 test of record or a rerun) the store lacks: everything its
   entry holds, and nothing else. #}
{% macro record_block(e, say) %}**{{ say.ledger_label }}** Replay `{{ e.run_id }}` (rules of commit `{{ e.freeze_commit|short }}`, code `{{ e.code_sha256|short }}`) is not in this copy's MLflow store: what follows comes from its entry in `docs/replay-ledger.json`, written from its run. MAPE of {{ e.mape|pct(2) }}, coverage of {{ e.coverage|pct(1) }}, recommendations: {{ recs_list(e.recommendations) }}; verdicts "{{ VERDICT[e.verdict.shipped] }}" against v1 as shipped and "{{ VERDICT[e.verdict.family] }}" against v1's form; label "{{ LABEL[e.evaluation] }}"; standing {% if e.standing %}"{{ OUTCOME[e.standing] }}"{% else %}none ({{ e.year }}){% endif %}; hash of the artifacts that judged it `{{ e.frozen_sha256|short }}`.{% if e.departure %} It departs from {% for x in e.departure_from %}`{{ x }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
